            plainText: "1. Fig. 1.3 shows Reiaan’s room with points OABC marking its corners. The x- and y-axes are marked in the figure. Point O is the origin. Fig. 1.3 Referring to Fig. 1.3, answer the following questions:(i) If D1R1 represents the door to Reiaan’s room, how far is the door from the left wall (the y-axis) of the room? How far is the door from the x-axis?(ii) What are the coordinates of D1?(iii) If R1 is the point (11.5, 0), how wide is the door? Do you think this is a comfortable width for the room door? If a person in a wheelchair wants to enter the room, will heshe be able to do so easily?(iv) If B1 (0, 1.5) and B2 (0, 4) represent the ends of the bathroom door, is the bathroom door narrower or wider than the room door? Fig. 1.3 From Fig. 1.3, the room door D₁R₁ is 1 unit away from the y-axis and 5 units above the x-axis.Therefore, distance of the door from the left wall (y-axis) = 1 ft and distance from the x-axis = 5 ft. ii) Coordinates of D₁ = (1, 5) Ans. iii) Given, R₁ = (11.5, 0) and D₁ = (1, 5).Width of the room door = 11.5 − 1 = 10.5 ft Ans.This is a wide door, so it should be comfortable for a person in a wheelchair. iv) Given, B₁ = (0, 1.5) and B₂ = (0, 4).Width of bathroom door = 4 − 1.5 = 2.5 ft.Since 2.5 ft < 10.5 ft, the bathroom door is narrower than the room door. Ans.",
