            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">7</span><span class=\"qtext\">If the length of a rectangle is three more than twice its width and its perimeter is 24 cm, what are the dimensions of the rectangle?</span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Let breadth = x cm.</span><span class=\"ln\">Length = (2x + 3) cm.</span><span class=\"ln\">Perimeter = 2(l+b)</span><span class=\"ln\">24 = 2[(2x+3)+x]</span><span class=\"ln\">⇒ 24 = 6x + 6</span><span class=\"ln\">⇒ x = 3</span><span class=\"ln\">∴ Breadth = <span class=\"box\">3 cm</span> and length = <span class=\"box\">9 cm</span>.</span>",
