        questions: [
          {
            id: "q1",
            number: "1",
            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">1</span><span class=\"qtext\"><span class=\"ln\">Draw the graphs of the following sets of lines. In each case, reflect on the role of ‘a’ and ‘b’.</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(i)</b> y = 4x, y = 2x, y = x</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(ii)</b> y = – 6x, y = – 3x, y = – x</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(iii)</b> y = 5x, y = –5x</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(iv)</b> y = 3x – 1, y = 3x, y = 3x + 1</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(v)</b> y = –2x – 3, y = –2x, y = 2x + 3</span></span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">i) y = 4x, y = 2x, y = x have y-intercept 0; their slopes are 4, 2 and 1 respectively.</span><span class=\"ln\">ii) y = −6x, y = −3x, y = −x have slopes −6, −3 and −1; all pass through the origin.</span><span class=\"ln\">iii) y = 5x and y = −5x have slopes 5 and −5; they are mirror lines about the y-axis.</span><span class=\"ln\">iv) y = 3x − 1, 3x, 3x + 1 have the same slope 3 and different y-intercepts −1, 0, 1, so they are parallel.</span><span class=\"ln\">v) y = −2x − 3, y = −2x, y = 2x + 3 have slopes −2, −2, 2; the first two are parallel.</span>",
            plainText: "1. Draw the graphs of the following sets of lines. In each case, reflect on the role of ‘a’ and ‘b’.(i) y = 4x, y = 2x, y = x(ii) y = – 6x, y = – 3x, y = – x(iii) y = 5x, y = –5x(iv) y = 3x – 1, y = 3x, y = 3x + 1(v) y = –2x – 3, y = –2x, y = 2x + 3 i) y = 4x, y = 2x, y = x have y-intercept 0; their slopes are 4, 2 and 1 respectively.ii) y = −6x, y = −3x, y = −x have slopes −6, −3 and −1; all pass through the origin.iii) y = 5x and y = −5x have slopes 5 and −5; they are mirror lines about the y-axis.iv) y = 3x − 1, 3x, 3x + 1 have the same slope 3 and different y-intercepts −1, 0, 1, so they are parallel.v) y = −2x − 3, y = −2x, y = 2x + 3 have slopes −2, −2, 2; the first two are parallel.",
          },
        ],
