            number: "★14",
            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">★14</span><span class=\"qtext\">What do all linear functions of the form f(x) = ax + a, a &gt; 0, have in common?</span>",
            body: "\n<span class=\"ln\">Given, f(x)=ax+a, a&gt;0</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">⇒ y=ax+a</span>\n<span class=\"ln\"><span class=\"given\">Here, slope = a and y-intercept = a.</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\">a&gt;0</span>\n<span class=\"ln arrow-step\">slope &gt; 0</span>\n<span class=\"ln imp-step\">it shows linear growth</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">f(x) will pass through positive y-axis.</span>\n<span class=\"ln tiny-gap\">For y=0,</span>\n<span class=\"ln arrow-step\">0=ax+a</span>\n<span class=\"ln arrow-step\">a(x+1)=0</span>\n<span class=\"ln arrow-step\">x+1=0</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">x=<span class=\"box\">−1</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln imp-step\">point of (x,y)=<span class=\"box\">(−1,0)</span> common.</span>\n",
