            body: "\n<span class=\"ln\"><b>i)</b> A debt multiplied by a fortune ⇒ the product of two debts is a debt.</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">The product of a fortune and a debt is a debt.</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">∴ (−12) × 5</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">= <span class=\"box\">−60</span> Ans.</span>\n<div class=\"part-divider\"></div>\n<span class=\"ln\"><b>ii)</b> The product of two debts is a fortune.</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">∴ (−8) × (−7)</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">= <span class=\"box\">56</span> Ans.</span>\n<div class=\"part-divider\"></div>\n<span class=\"ln\"><b>iii)</b> Zero minus a debt is the same no. but positive.</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">A debt subtracted from zero, it be a fortune.</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">∴ 0 − (−14)</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">= 0 + 14</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">= <span class=\"box\">14</span></span>\n<div class=\"part-divider\"></div>\n<span class=\"ln\"><b>iv)</b> (−20) ÷ 4</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">The quotient of a debt and a fortune is a debt.</span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">∴ <span class=\"f\"><span class=\"n\">−20</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span></span>\n<span class=\"ln indent\">= <span class=\"box\">−5</span></span>\n",
