            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">1</span><span class=\"qtext\"><span class=\"ln\">Draw ΔABC with AB = 5 cm, ∠A = 70° and ∠B = 60°. Draw the circumcircle of ΔABC. Is the centre inside or outside the triangle?</span></span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Construction: Draw AB = 5 cm. At A construct ∠A = 70° and at B construct ∠B = 60°. The two rays meet at C.</span><div style=\"margin:12px 0 18px;display:flex;justify-content:center;overflow-x:auto;\"><svg height=\"220\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;background:#fffdf3;border:1px solid #d8cfb5;border-radius:8px;\" viewbox=\"0 0 520 220\" width=\"520\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"85\" x2=\"430\" y1=\"175\" y2=\"175\"></line><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"85\" x2=\"210\" y1=\"175\" y2=\"55\"></line><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"430\" x2=\"210\" y1=\"175\" y2=\"55\"></line><circle cx=\"247\" cy=\"145\" fill=\"none\" r=\"132\" stroke=\"#b3372c\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\" stroke-width=\"2\"></circle><line stroke=\"#c99a3f\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" stroke-width=\"2\" x1=\"210\" x2=\"210\" y1=\"55\" y2=\"175\"></line><line stroke=\"#c99a3f\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" stroke-width=\"2\" x1=\"257\" x2=\"257\" y1=\"175\" y2=\"55\"></line><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"78\" y=\"198\">A</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"425\" y=\"198\">B</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"204\" y=\"43\">C</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"250\" y=\"142\">O</text><text font-size=\"15\" x=\"195\" y=\"215\">acute triangle + circumcircle</text></svg></div><span class=\"ln\">∠C = 180° − 70° − 60° = 50°.</span><span class=\"ln\">All three angles are less than 90°, so ΔABC is an acute-angled triangle.</span><span class=\"ln\">Construct the perpendicular bisectors of two sides. Their intersection is the circumcentre O inside the triangle.</span><span class=\"ln\">Therefore, the circumcentre lies <span class=\"box\">inside</span> the triangle.</span>",
            plainText: "1. Draw ΔABC with AB = 5 cm, ∠A = 70° and ∠B = 60°. Draw the circumcircle of ΔABC. Is the centre inside or outside the triangle? Construction: Draw AB = 5 cm. At A construct ∠A = 70° and at B construct ∠B = 60°. The two rays meet at C.ABCOacute triangle + circumcircle ∠C = 180° − 70° − 60° = 50°.All three angles are less than 90°, so ΔABC is an acute-angled triangle.Construct the perpendicular bisectors of two sides. Their intersection is the circumcentre O inside the triangle.Therefore, the circumcentre lies inside the triangle.",
