            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Construction: Draw AB = 6 cm. With A and B as centres and radius 7 cm, draw arcs intersecting at C. Join AC and BC.</span><div style=\"margin:12px 0 18px;display:flex;justify-content:center;overflow-x:auto;\"><svg height=\"220\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;background:#fffdf3;border:1px solid #d8cfb5;border-radius:8px;\" viewbox=\"0 0 520 220\" width=\"520\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"112\" x2=\"408\" y1=\"180\" y2=\"180\"></line><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"112\" x2=\"260\" y1=\"180\" y2=\"62\"></line><line stroke=\"#213575\" stroke-width=\"3\" x1=\"408\" x2=\"260\" y1=\"180\" y2=\"62\"></line><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"151\" fill=\"none\" r=\"150\" stroke=\"#b3372c\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\" stroke-width=\"2\"></circle><line stroke=\"#c99a3f\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" stroke-width=\"2\" x1=\"260\" x2=\"260\" y1=\"62\" y2=\"180\"></line><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"151\" fill=\"#c99a3f\" r=\"4\"></circle><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"101\" y=\"202\">A</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"404\" y=\"202\">B</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"253\" y=\"50\">C</text><text font-size=\"18\" x=\"267\" y=\"148\">O</text><text font-size=\"15\" x=\"180\" y=\"215\">AB=6, AC=BC=7</text></svg></div><span class=\"ln\">Since BC = CA = 7 cm, the triangle is isosceles.</span><span class=\"ln\">Construct the perpendicular bisectors of the sides. Their intersection gives the circumcentre O.</span><span class=\"ln\">Measuring the radii gives OA ≈ OB ≈ OC.</span><span class=\"ln\">OA ≈ OB ≈ OC ≈ <span class=\"box\">3.85 cm</span>.</span>",
            plainText: "3. Draw ΔABC, with AB = 6 cm, BC = 7 cm and CA = 7 cm. Draw the circumcircle of ΔABC. Let the circumcentre be O. Measure OA, OB, OC. Construction: Draw AB = 6 cm. With A and B as centres and radius 7 cm, draw arcs intersecting at C. Join AC and BC.ABCOAB=6, AC=BC=7 Since BC = CA = 7 cm, the triangle is isosceles.Construct the perpendicular bisectors of the sides. Their intersection gives the circumcentre O.Measuring the radii gives OA ≈ OB ≈ OC.OA ≈ OB ≈ OC ≈ 3.85 cm.",
