            plainText: "4. A circle has a radius of 15 cm. A chord is drawn. The distance from the centre of the circle to the chord is 9 cm. What is the length of the chord? Given, r = 15 cm and d = 9 cm.Half chord = √(15² − 9²) = √144 = 12 cm.Therefore, chord length = 24 cm Ans.",
