            id: "q23",
            number: "★23",
            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">★23</span><span class=\"qtext\"><span class=\"ln\">Let A be any point within a given circle with centre O. Show that the shortest chord of the circle that passes through point A is the one that is perpendicular to OA.</span></span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Let a chord through A have perpendicular distance d from O.</span><span class=\"ln\">Its length is 2√(R² − d²).</span><span class=\"ln\">For a line through A, the greatest possible perpendicular distance from O is OA, and this occurs when the chord is perpendicular to OA.</span><span class=\"ln\">A larger d gives a smaller chord.</span><span class=\"ln\">Therefore, the shortest chord through A is the one <span class=\"box\">perpendicular to OA</span>.</span>",
            plainText: "★23. Let A be any point within a given circle with centre O. Show that the shortest chord of the circle that passes through point A is the one that is perpendicular to OA. Let a chord through A have perpendicular distance d from O.Its length is 2√(R² − d²).For a line through A, the greatest possible perpendicular distance from O is OA, and this occurs when the chord is perpendicular to OA.A larger d gives a smaller chord.Therefore, the shortest chord through A is the one perpendicular to OA.",
