            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">★25</span><span class=\"qtext\"><span class=\"ln\">In a circle, two chords CC' and DD' are drawn perpendicular to a diameter AB. Prove that the segment MM' joining the midpoints of the chords CD and C' D' is perpendicular to AB.</span></span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Let the chords CD and C'D' be perpendicular to diameter AB, with M and M' their midpoints.</span><span class=\"ln\">Since the perpendicular from the centre to a chord bisects it, OM ⟂ CD and OM′ ⟂ C′D′.</span><span class=\"ln\">Both M and M′ lie on the perpendicular bisectors of their respective chords.</span><span class=\"ln\">Because CD and C′D′ are parallel to each other and both perpendicular to AB, their midpoints lie on a line <span class=\"box\">perpendicular to AB</span>.</span>",
            plainText: "★25. In a circle, two chords CC' and DD' are drawn perpendicular to a diameter AB. Prove that the segment MM' joining the midpoints of the chords CD and C' D' is perpendicular to AB. Let the chords CD and C'D' be perpendicular to diameter AB, with M and M' their midpoints.Since the perpendicular from the centre to a chord bisects it, OM ⟂ CD and OM′ ⟂ C′D′.Both M and M′ lie on the perpendicular bisectors of their respective chords.Because CD and C′D′ are parallel to each other and both perpendicular to AB, their midpoints lie on a line perpendicular to AB.",
