            body: "<div class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"data:image/jpegpng;base64,\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ln center\"><i>Fig. 5.31</i></div></div><span class=\"ln\">Join the centre O to all four vertices.</span><span class=\"ln\">Radii of the circle are equal, so triangles formed by the radii are isosceles.</span><span class=\"ln\">Let the angles at A, B, C and D be p, q, u and v as shown.</span><span class=\"ln\">Using the angle sum in the isosceles triangles around O, the four angles of the cyclic quadrilateral add to <span class=\"box\">180°</span>.</span><span class=\"ln\">Hence, the sum of each pair of opposite angles is <span class=\"box\">180°</span>.</span>",
