            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">5</span><span class=\"qtext\"><span class=\"ln\">A ball is dropped from a height of 80 metres. After hitting the ground, it bounces back to 60% of the height from which it fell. It continues bouncing in this way — each time rising to 60% of the previous height.</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(i)</b> What height does the ball reach after the 5th bounce?</span><span class=\"ln\"><b>(ii)</b> What is the total vertical distance the ball has travelled by the time it hits the ground for the 6th time?</span></span>",
            body: "<span class=\"ln\">Initial height = 80 m and r=0.6.</span><span class=\"ln\">i) Height after 5th bounce = 80(0.6)⁵ = <span class=\"box\">6.2208 m</span>.</span><span class=\"ln\">ii) Total distance till the 6th hit = 80 + 2×80(0.6+0.6²+0.6³+0.6⁴+0.6⁵)</span><span class=\"ln\">= <span class=\"box\">230.3104 m</span>.</span>",
            plainText: "5. A ball is dropped from a height of 80 metres. After hitting the ground, it bounces back to 60% of the height from which it fell. It continues bouncing in this way — each time rising to 60% of the previous height.(i) What height does the ball reach after the 5th bounce?(ii) What is the total vertical distance the ball has travelled by the time it hits the ground for the 6th time? Initial height = 80 m and r=0.6.i) Height after 5th bounce = 80(0.6)⁵ = 6.2208 m.ii) Total distance till the 6th hit = 80 + 2×80(0.6+0.6²+0.6³+0.6⁴+0.6⁵)= 230.3104 m.",
