            head: "<span class=\"qnum\">★14</span><span class=\"qtext\">Suppose P1 = 1, P2 = 2 and for n &gt; 2, Pn = P1 + P2 + … + Pn–1 + 1. Find the values of P1, P2, …, P8. Can you find a simpler recursive formula for Pn? Can you give an explicit formula?</span>",
            body: "\n<span class=\"ln\">P₁=1, P₂=2</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">P₃=P₁+P₂+1=1+2+1=<span class=\"box\">4</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\">P₄=1+2+4+1=<span class=\"box\">8</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\">P₅=1+2+4+8+1=<span class=\"box\">16</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\">Therefore,</span>\n<span class=\"ln center\"><span class=\"box\">P₁,P₂,…,P₈ = 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\">Simpler recursive formula: <span class=\"box\">Pₙ=2Pₙ₋₁</span>, n&gt;2.</span>\n<span class=\"ln\">Explicit formula: <span class=\"box\">Pₙ=2ⁿ⁻¹</span>.</span>\n",
            plainText: "★14. Suppose P1 = 1, P2 = 2 and for n > 2, Pn = P1 + P2 + … + Pn–1 + 1. Find the values of P1, P2, …, P8. Can you find a simpler recursive formula for Pn? Can you give an explicit formula? P₁=1, P₂=2 P₃=P₁+P₂+1=1+2+1=4 P₄=1+2+4+1=8 P₅=1+2+4+8+1=16 Therefore, P₁,P₂,…,P₈ = 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128 Simpler recursive formula: Pₙ=2Pₙ₋₁, n>2. Explicit formula: Pₙ=2ⁿ⁻¹.",
